WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590
The Torah begins with
a single letter: bet.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.620
It is closed on three sides,
and open only forward.

3
00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.410
From its shape, the rabbis drew a lesson.

4
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.600
Don't speculate about
what came before creation.

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.540
Look at what follows.

6
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.260
That is a lot to find in one letter.

7
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.260
So how can one verse of the
Torah have four meanings at once?

8
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.690
In this mission, you'll search
the text the way the rabbis did:

9
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.990
filling gaps, and explaining repeats.

10
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.570
Then you'll weigh up which
matters more in Judaism:

11
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.710
the law, or the story.

12
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: find out how one verse of
the Torah can hold four meanings at once.
